  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_ANIMALKINGDOM_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Cross-sectional view of diploblastic germinal layers</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The given cross-sectional diagram represents the embryonic germinal layer organisation of a diploblastic animal. Identify the undifferentiated layer labelled <strong>Q</strong> and select the phylum that exhibits this organisation.</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 240" width="320" height="240" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="320" height="240" fill="#ffffff"/>
          <!-- Outer ectoderm ring -->
          <circle cx="130" cy="120" r="85" fill="#b8b5e8" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Middle undifferentiated layer (Mesoglea) -->
          <circle cx="130" cy="120" r="62" fill="#f87171" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Inner endoderm ring -->
          <circle cx="130" cy="120" r="40" fill="#d1d5db" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Central lumen -->
          <circle cx="130" cy="120" r="24" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Pointer lines and labels -->
          <line x1="185" y1="65" x2="245" y2="45" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="185" cy="65" r="2.5" fill="#111827"/>
          <text x="252" y="50" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">P (Cellular)</text>

          <line x1="182" y1="120" x2="245" y2="120" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="182" cy="120" r="2.5" fill="#111827"/>
          <text x="252" y="125" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Q (Non-cellular)</text>

          <line x1="162" y1="145" x2="245" y2="185" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="162" cy="145" r="2.5" fill="#111827"/>
          <text x="252" y="190" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">R (Cellular)</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram shows a transverse cross-section of a diploblastic animal body plan consisting of three concentric regions around a central cavity: an outer cellular layer labelled <strong>P</strong>, a middle non-cellular undifferentiated layer labelled <strong>Q</strong>, and an inner cellular layer labelled <strong>R</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>In cross-sectional anatomical diagrams of embryonic germinal layers, layers are interpreted radially from the outermost body surface inward toward the central gastro-vascular lumen.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>Diploblastic animals have cells arranged in two embryonic layers—an external ectoderm and an internal endoderm—with an undifferentiated, non-cellular layer called mesoglea present between them. Coelenterates (Cnidarians) exhibit this organisation.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. The outermost cellular layer <strong>P</strong> represents the ectoderm.<br/>2. The innermost cellular layer <strong>R</strong> lining the central cavity represents the endoderm.<br/>3. The middle undifferentiated layer <strong>Q</strong> located between the ectoderm and endoderm is the mesoglea.<br/>4. Phyla such as Platyhelminthes, Aschelminthes, and Annelida are triploblastic (possessing a cellular mesoderm), whereas Coelenterata (Cnidaria) is diploblastic.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Confirming against the diploblastic body plan, the undifferentiated middle layer is mesoglea and the representative phylum is Coelenterata (Cnidaria). Therefore, the correct identification is Mesoglea; Coelenterata (Cnidaria).</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Mesoderm; Platyhelminthes</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Mesoglea; Coelenterata (Cnidaria)</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Mesoglea; Annelida</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Endoderm; Aschelminthes</p>]]></text></answer>
