  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_ANIMALKINGDOM_DIAGRAM_Q04 - Broad classification flowchart of Kingdom Animalia</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>In the given broad classification flowchart of Kingdom Animalia, identify <strong>X</strong>, <strong>Y</strong>, and <strong>Z</strong> correctly.</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 320" width="560" height="320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="560" height="320" fill="#fef9c3"/>
          <!-- Column Headers -->
          <text x="15" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Kingdom</text>
          <text x="115" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Organisation</text>
          <text x="230" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Symmetry</text>
          <text x="320" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Body Cavity</text>
          <text x="455" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Phylum</text>

          <!-- Kingdom -->
          <text x="15" y="130" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Animalia</text>
          <text x="15" y="145" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">(multicellular)</text>

          <!-- Branch from Animalia -->
          <path d="M 90 130 L 105 130 M 105 60 L 105 180 M 105 60 L 115 60 M 105 180 L 115 180" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>

          <!-- Cellular level -->
          <text x="118" y="64" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Cellular level</text>
          <line x1="190" y1="60" x2="225" y2="60" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="228" y="64" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Asymmetrical</text>
          <line x1="300" y1="60" x2="320" y2="60" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="323" y="64" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Acoelomata</text>
          <line x1="390" y1="60" x2="450" y2="60" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="455" y="64" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Porifera</text>

          <!-- Tissue/Organ/Organ system -->
          <text x="118" y="176" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Tissue/Organ/</text>
          <text x="118" y="190" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Organ system</text>

          <!-- Branch to Radial and Bilateral -->
          <path d="M 195 180 L 215 180 M 215 110 L 215 220 M 215 110 L 228 110 M 215 220 L 228 220" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>

          <!-- Radial -->
          <text x="232" y="114" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Radial</text>
          <line x1="270" y1="110" x2="318" y2="110" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="320" y="98" width="42" height="22" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="336" y="114" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#dc2626">X</text>
          <path d="M 362 110 L 435 110 M 435 95 L 435 125 M 435 95 L 450 95 M 435 125 L 450 125" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="455" y="99" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Coelenterata</text>
          <text x="455" y="129" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Ctenophora</text>

          <!-- Bilateral -->
          <text x="232" y="224" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Bilateral</text>
          <path d="M 280 220 L 302 220 M 302 165 L 302 265 M 302 165 L 318 165 M 302 205 L 318 205 M 302 265 L 318 265" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>

          <!-- Without body cavity -->
          <text x="322" y="169" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Without body cavity</text>
          <line x1="428" y1="165" x2="450" y2="165" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="455" y="169" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Platyhelminthes</text>

          <!-- With false coelom -->
          <text x="322" y="209" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">With false coelom</text>
          <line x1="422" y1="205" x2="450" y2="205" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="453" y="193" width="42" height="22" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="469" y="209" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#dc2626">Y</text>

          <!-- With true coelom -->
          <text x="322" y="269" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">With true coelom</text>
          <path d="M 418 265 L 435 265 M 435 235 L 435 295 M 435 235 L 450 235 M 435 265 L 450 265 M 435 295 L 450 295" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="455" y="239" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Annelida, Arthropoda</text>
          <text x="455" y="269" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Mollusca, </text>
          <rect x="506" y="253" width="38" height="22" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="520" y="269" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#dc2626">*Z</text>
          <text x="455" y="299" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Hemichordata, Chordata</text>

          <!-- Footnote -->
          <text x="15" y="310" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="10" font-style="italic" fill="#374151">*Exhibits radial symmetry in adults and bilateral symmetry in larvae.</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The classification flowchart divides Kingdom Animalia based on levels of organisation, body symmetry, and nature of the body cavity (coelom), with three missing entries: <strong>X</strong> (body cavity category for radially symmetrical Coelenterata and Ctenophora), <strong>Y</strong> (phylum with bilateral symmetry and false coelom), and <strong>Z</strong> (coelomate phylum marked with an asterisk indicating radial symmetry in adults and bilateral symmetry in larvae).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>Each horizontal path from left to right in the flowchart pairs a level of organisation with its corresponding symmetry, coelom type, and representative phyla.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>1. Coelenterata and Ctenophora are diploblastic, radially symmetrical animals lacking a body cavity (acoelomates).<br/>2. Aschelminthes are bilaterally symmetrical animals with a false coelom (pseudocoelomates).<br/>3. Echinodermata are true coelomates in which larvae are bilaterally symmetrical while adults exhibit radial symmetry.</p>
